# CODEX-b projected HNL sensitivity, |U_{eN}|^2 single-flavour dominance
# Source: arXiv:1911.00481v2 (CODEX-b Expression of Interest), fig:Ne_combined
# Source figure PDF: sources/arXiv-1911.00481/HNL_Ele.pdf
# Method: vector extraction from Mathematica PDF path operators;
#   log-axis calibration from TICK GEOMETRY (not tick-label text bboxes).
#   x 150.3947 pt/decade, y 32.1590 pt/decade;
#   frame spans m = 0.2 .. 49.99 GeV.
# Curve colour: RGB(1.00,0.55,0.00), confirmed against the legend swatch.
# Nature: the EoI quotes DIRAC HNLs. Column 2 is the Majorana contour,
#   as the CODEX-b authors prescribe (S. Knapen, 2026-10-05): lower-edge
#   vertices / sqrt2, lifetime-limited upper-edge vertices / 2, tip at the
#   Dirac tip mass. With equal production and Gamma_M = 2 Gamma_D at fixed
#   U^2, N_M(U^2) = N_D(2 U^2)/2: the lower edge (N ~ U^4) moves by exactly
#   1/sqrt2; U^2/2 on the upper edge keeps the lifetime but drops the halved
#   production, so it is the outer bound of the Majorana island (the exact
#   edge lies lower by a relative ~ln2/(a U^2), a few per cent).
#   The frame vertex at the top has no Majorana value (NaN).
#   Column 3 is the unconverted value as drawn in the source figure.
#   Drop a column's NaN rows to get its polyline.
# Contour is open: it exits the frame at the left edge (low mass) and
#   through the top edge (short lifetime); the region is closed by the
#   plot border in the original, so no closure chord is stored here, and
#   the Majorana curve ends at the last column below the frame top.
# Best reach (Dirac, as drawn): U^2 = 1.8798e-08 at m_N = 1.5 GeV
# Best reach (Majorana): U^2 = 1.3292e-08 at m_N = 1.5 GeV
